@startuml agent_tool_permission_cache
title Managed Runtime Tool Permission Cache
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java@80ca6cc96d35fef2aa86bbd032a980945db4ecbd.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/MateServiceClient.java AgentRuntime, SkillInfo, BoundTool.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java writeSkills, loadSkill, toSettings, toRuntime, validSettings, validCachedSkill.
' Implementation commit: pi-mono-java@2b76bbf9.
' Pi baseline: pi-mono@4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3 has no matching managed permission cache.
' Observed behavior: the source baseline discarded Agent and Skill bindingTools while writing and loading the managed snapshot.
' Security hardening: missing permission fields invalidate the snapshot, while explicit empty arrays remain valid.
' Design reason: a trusted fixed permission snapshot must survive publication, cache hits, and process restarts.

actor Mate
participant AgentRuntimeManager as Manager
database "Staging directory" as Staging
database "Published directory" as Cache
participant PreparedAgentRuntime as Prepared
participant "Permission policy" as Policy

Mate -> Manager: AgentRuntime and SkillInfo\nwith bindingTools
Manager -> Staging: Write settings.json\nand skill.json arrays
Manager -> Staging: Validate complete snapshot
Manager -> Cache: Atomic publish

Manager -> Cache: Read managed snapshot
alt bindingTools field is missing or invalid
    Cache --> Manager: Incomplete snapshot
    Manager --> Manager: prepareCached returns empty
    Manager -> Mate: prepare refetches snapshot
else bindingTools is present, including empty array
    Cache --> Manager: Complete snapshot
    Manager -> Prepared: Restore exact BoundTool records
    Prepared -> Policy: Fixed Agent and Skill permissions
    note right of Policy
      ASK requires an explicit trusted value.
      Unknown or conflicting values are DENY.
      Tool schemas are not cached here.
    end note
end
@enduml
